= The Bárcenas Papers

In a shocking revelation, the El Mundo and El País newspapers have published leaked documents from the PP's former treasurer, Luis Bárceas under the leadership of Presidente José María Aznar. In these hand-written documents and notes, the PP's top leadership and close associates are shown to have been receiving large sums of money in cash. The supposed white envelopes would have included monthly under-the-table payments of up to €15.000 per person.

The party has not only denied any wrongdoing and challenged the authenticity of the documents, but also risen tensions with the former treasurer who, on his side, has now sued the party for improperly dismissing him. The trials for the now called "Bárcenas Case" are expected to be long and complex to say the least.

- @post_event: PP corruption is hardly shocking though...
